text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6B6152\" class=\"c-dim\">08-26</text><text x=\"515.1\" y=\"392\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6B6152\" class=\"c-dim\">11-11</text><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"610\" y1=\"166.9\" y2=\"166.9\" stroke=\"#6B6152\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"616\" y=\"170.9\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#6B6152\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">$560.57</tspan> 61.8% retrace</text><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"610\" y1=\"204.0\" y2=\"204.0\" stroke=\"#2F6E4A\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"616\" y=\"208.0\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#2F6E4A\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">$530.31</tspan> 50% retrace</text><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"610\" y1=\"241.1\" y2=\"241.1\" stroke=\"#6B6152\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"616\" y=\"245.1\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#6B6152\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">$500.05</tspan> 38.2% retrace</text><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"610\" y1=\"339.4\" y2=\"339.4\" stroke=\"#1B8FA8\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"616\" y=\"343.4\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#1B8FA8\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">$420.05</tspan> 200-day avg</text><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"610\" y1=\"361.4\" y2=\"361.4\" stroke=\"#A63A2E\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"616\" y=\"365.4\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#A63A2E\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">$402.10</tspan> Nov low</text><circle cx=\"515.1\" cy=\"176.3\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#C9A84C\" stroke=\"#20242C\" stroke-width=\"1\"/></svg></figure>\n<p>These lines are mine, not yours. You have not sent Fib levels for AMD.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Trend:</strong> up. Close $552.90 (Nov 11), above the 20-day ($517.60), just above the 50-day ($550.43) and far above the 200-day ($420.05).</li><li><strong>Momentum:</strong> RSI 53.6. Neutral, neither stretched nor washed out.</li><li><strong>Ceiling:</strong> $560.57, the 61.8% retracement of the drop from $658.52 (Oct 6, also the 52-week high) to $402.10 (Nov 5). The Nov 11 high was $567.65 and the close fell back under the line. Above that, $579.18 (Oct 28 high), then $658.52.</li><li><strong>Floor:</strong> $530.31 (50% retracement), then the 20-day at $517.60 and $500.05 (38.2%). The swing low is $402.10. The 52-week low is $188.22 (Mar 3).</li><li><strong>Your tested edge:</strong> does not apply. The uptrend half is there (price and 50-day above the 200-day), but RSI is 53.6, not under 40. It did apply on Nov 2–4 and Nov 6 (RSI 34.6 to 39.5, price above the 200-day); that moment has passed.</li><li><strong>Scorecard:</strong> no open or watching play on AMD.</li><li><strong>Verdict:</strong> the chart supports the upside, with one step left. A close above $560.57 says the drop is being fully repaired. A close below $500.05 flips the read to down and puts $402.10 back in view. That agrees with what management described: the raise is real and the trend is intact, and the chart has already taken back more than half of the fall.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"what-would-change-this-read\">What would change this read</h3>\n<ul><li>The next report (date not found). Watch the gross margin against the 55% guide and whether Q4 lands near $17B.</li><li>Memory: a second cut to the margin guide, or word that memory supply is capping MI450 and Helios shipments. Micron's next report (quarter ends around Nov 30) is the early signal.</li><li>Nvidia on Nov 17. If its supply commitments grew again, there is less memory left for everyone else.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"confidence-and-sources\">Confidence and sources</h3>\n<p>Solid: results, guidance and filing figures (company release, 10-Q). Medium: call detail, which came from a machine-translated transcript read in part. Thin: succession and share-structure detail, because the full proxy statement was not opened; the next report date; any backlog figure. The TrendForce 121% figure is from a headline, not the full article.</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://ir.amd.com/news-events/press-releases/detail/1303/amd-reports-third-quarter-2